-- title:
--   Igusa monodromy: SL₂(ℤ/M) lies in the image
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field and $M$ a nonzero natural number whose image in $K$ is nonzero. Let $k$ and $\Omega$ be fields, both $K$-algebras, with $\Omega$ a $k$-algebra compatibly with these structures, and with $\Omega$ an algebraic closure of $k$. Let $E$ be a Weierstrass curve over $k$ that is elliptic, and assume its $j$-invariant $E.j$ is transcendental over $K$ and generates $k$ over $K$, in the sense that the intermediate field $K(E.j)$ of $k$ is all of $k$. Let $P_1,P_2$ be points of the affine model of the base change of $E$ to $\Omega$, each killed by $M$, and independent in the sense that for integers $a,b$ the relation $aP_1+bP_2=0$ forces $M \mid a$ and $M \mid b$; thus $P_1,P_2$ is a basis of $E[M](\Omega)$. Let $a,b,c,d$ be integers with $M \mid ad-bc-1$. The conclusion is that there exists a $k$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $\Omega$ such that the induced map on points sends $P_1$ to $aP_1+cP_2$ and $P_2$ to $bP_1+dP_2$.
--
--   This is the full-image form of Igusa's monodromy theorem for the elliptic curve with transcendental (generic) $j$-invariant: the image of $\mathrm{Aut}(\Omega/k)$ in $\mathrm{Aut}(E[M]) \cong \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/M)$ contains every matrix of determinant $1$, written here on the basis $P_1,P_2$ with $\sigma$ acting by the matrix with columns $(a,c)$ and $(b,d)$; only this inclusion is asserted, not the equality with $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/M)$ that the Weil pairing gives over an algebraically closed base. It is used to bound the index of subgroups of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/N)$ by the degree of the field generated by the corresponding $j$-invariant, in the results on full-level modular curves that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_algEquiv_map_eq_zsmul_add_zsmul_of_transcendental_j.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open WeierstrassCurve.Affine
open WeierstrassCurve

universe u v in

theorem WeierstrassCurve.exists_algEquiv_map_eq_zsmul_add_zsmul_of_transcendental_j
    (K : Type u) [Field K] [IsAlgClosed K] (M : ℕ) [NeZero M] (hM : (M : K) ≠ 0)
    (k Ω : Type v) [Field k] [Field Ω] [DecidableEq Ω] [Algebra K k] [Algebra K Ω] [Algebra k Ω]
    [IsScalarTower K k Ω] [IsAlgClosure k Ω] (E : WeierstrassCurve k) [E.IsElliptic]
    (hE : Transcendental K E.j) (hgen : IntermediateField.adjoin K ({E.j} : Set k) = ⊤)
    (P₁ P₂ : (E.baseChange Ω).toAffine.Point) (hP₁ : M • P₁ = 0) (hP₂ : M • P₂ = 0)
    (hind : ∀ a b : ℤ, a • P₁ + b • P₂ = 0 → (M : ℤ) ∣ a ∧ (M : ℤ) ∣ b)
    (a b c d : ℤ) (hdet : (M : ℤ) ∣ a * d - b * c - 1) :
    ∃ σ : Ω ≃ₐ[k] Ω,
      WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point.map (σ : Ω →ₐ[k] Ω) P₁ = a • P₁ + c • P₂ ∧
      WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point.map (σ : Ω →ₐ[k] Ω) P₂ = b • P₁ + d • P₂ := by sorry
